  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0 — first release. Extracted from the Bonder monolith so on-premise sync\nagents can be developed and shipped without access to Bonder's source.\n\nContents:\n\n* Entity interfaces that push data into Bonder over the public API and\n  reconcile it against what is already there: customers, contacts, partners,\n  products, product groups, product items, installation sites, groups and\n  components, assets, contracts, appointments, support cases, support teams,\n  support activities, actions and life-log entries.\n* The matching BcInterface* DTOs, keyed by a caller-chosen reference field\n  (for example a CustomData field) so an agent can address Bonder records by\n  the source system's own identifiers.\n* BonderAgentConfigStore and BonderAgentConfiguration — the agent's .bonderrc:\n  endpoint, tenant, cached token and a CustomData slot agents use for their\n  sync cursor. The file format is the one the Bonder CLI writes, including the\n  legacy single-object shape and the endpoint ordinal, so an agent that drops\n  the CLI in favour of this package keeps its token and its cursor.\n* BonderClientRegistrationModule, which registers a logged-in BonderClient in\n  an IServiceCollection with token renewal and full re-login on failure.\n* On-prem ingest helpers (OnPremIngestClient, IngestRowsZipBuilder,\n  ImportMappingSeeder) and the mass-import throttle.\n\nTargets netstandard2.0. Depends on Bonder.Net.Client 1.3.0.",
